{"item_id": "BM0001", "category": "numerical", "subtopic": "binomial probability", "difficulty": "intro", "answer_type": "number", "preferred_letter": "", "question": "A fair six-sided die is rolled 5 times. Let X be the number of times a 6 appears. Find P(X = 2). Give your answer to 3 decimal places.", "choices": [], "r_solution": "cat(dbinom(2, size = 5, prob = 1/6))", "canonical_answer": "0.161", "answer_tolerance": 0.0005, "r_check": "", "explanation": "X ~ Binomial(5, 1/6), so P(X=2) = choose(5,2)(1/6)^2(5/6)^3 = 0.1608.", "problems": []}
